carld@ms.uky.edu (Carl Lafferty) writes:

>I have been
>playing Nethack for 6 years in various incarnations and only won the
>game ONE time and I use save files!  I think the game is hard enough
>without having to start over if you screw up with one single mistake.

This is actually the reason why I *don't* use save files:  you won't
learn your lessons well unless you SUFFER for them.  With save files,
you never need to learn all the intricacies of the game, because you
can survive without them (eventually).  A friend of mine uses save
files, and has gone much further than I have into the dungeon - but my
characters survive MUCH better than his do.  He'll take that last
hopeful hack while on 2HP, but I'll stop and pour over my inventory for
a minute or so, sum up the risks, look at my discoveries and notes,
then finally turn an un-identified wand on myself (or the enemy).  


